      "title_size": "sm",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Coverage at a glance",
      "order": 2,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "center",
      "body": "Depth from mosdepth, per amplicon and per genome position. The amplicon view is the one that finds primer dropout: a scheme drops one amplicon in a handful of samples long before whole-genome breadth moves. The threshold card counts how many amplicon measurements sit under 20x, which is the floor a consensus base call needs.",
      "wf_tag": "nextflow/viralrecon"
    },
