      "parent_index": null,
      "last_updated": "2026-08-29T00:00:00.000000",
      "title_size": "sm",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Coverage tracks",
      "order": 2,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "center",
      "body": "The genome track is per position, one lane per sample, so a dropout reads as a gap. The amplicon track below it is the same data binned by amplicon on a log axis, which is the view that names the amplicon responsible. The clustered heatmap puts samples in rows and amplicons in columns: a vertical dark band is a scheme problem, a horizontal one is a sample problem.",
      "wf_tag": "nextflow/viralrecon"
    },
